<% content_for(:title, "Portfolio · McRitchie Studio") %>
<% content_for(:full_width, true) %>

<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 text-center section-padding">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-heading tracking-tight">Portfolio</h1>
  <p class="text-secondary text-lg mt-4 leading-relaxed">Real apps, live today. Open one and look around.</p>
</section>

<%# The apps ride the engine's carousel (studio/_carousel), the apps' standard for a
    set too long to grid, in its cascade style (Alex McRitchie, 2026-11-08): a looping
    3D stack, the open app in front and two each side stepping back (three on a phone).
    portfolio_carousel_style picks it once the installed engine has it (task
    carousel-cascade-style) and keeps the spotlight on an engine before it.
    Each slide is the app's still and nothing else (websites/_portfolio_card); the open
    card wears a violet ring. The open app's name, host and blurb are ONE caption under
    the stack (websites/_portfolio_caption, a stack of one per app in one place),
    which cross-fades in place as the row moves: a caption inside a slide would ride
    the slide's 3D move, so portfolio_captions.js follows the engine's open-slide
    marker (data-current) instead. The prev and next arrows flank the stack; the row
    has no dots (portfolio-row, build_cards.css). No autoplay (Alex McRitchie,
    2026-11-08, "we can drop this" of the dots and the pause button): moving content
    owes a visible pause (WCAG 2.2.2), so the arrows, a swipe or drag and a click on
    a side card move it. The loop asks through carousel_optional_locals, which passes
    only the locals the installed studio/_carousel declares. /build keeps its own
    gallery card. %>
<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4" style="padding-bottom: 4rem;">
  <div class="portfolio-stage" data-portfolio-stage>
    <%= render layout: "studio/carousel",
          locals: { label: "Live apps", items: @examples, per_view: 3, id: "websites-apps", style: portfolio_carousel_style, class_name: "portfolio-row",
                    slide_label: ->(example) { example.name }, data: { test: "websites-carousel" } }
                    .merge(carousel_optional_locals(loop: true)) do |example| %>
      <%= render "websites/portfolio_card", example: example %>
    <% end %>
    <div class="portfolio-captions" data-portfolio-captions>
      <% @examples.each_with_index do |example, index| %>
        <%= render "websites/portfolio_caption", example: example, current: index.zero? %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
  <%# Just under the caption, centred (Alex McRitchie, 2026-11-08). %>
  <div class="mt-4 text-center">
    <%= link_to "Build Your Website", build_path, class: "btn btn-primary", data: { test: "websites-build-cta" } %>
  </div>
</div>
